You will need
- Node.js 20+
- Python 3.12
- PostgreSQL 15+ running locally

1. Get the latest project
git clone "https://github.com/RADIANT-NOODLE/Group8Project.git"
cd Group8Project
but if you already cloned it git pull is fine

2. Create the database (once, in psql)
    CREATE USER valora_user WITH PASSWORD 'valora_password';
    CREATE DATABASE valora_db OWNER valora_user;

3. Start the backend (from the backend folder)
    python -m venv .venv  and activate it
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    copy .env.example .env
    python -m alembic upgrade head
    python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8000

4. Start the frontend (from the FrontEnd folder)
    npm install
    npm run dev

5. You can now open valora:
-Frontend:
http://localhost:4173

-Backend:
http://localhost:8000

-API documentation:
http://localhost:8000/docs


6. Test the actual system, create accounts and log in & out.
It should create actual records on the local PostgreSQL database and the login should return a JWT
Estate agent accounts are created by an HOA admin (Create Agent Account), not by registering.

